# Galaxy S26 only: the llama.cpp Gemma 4 E2B text cells (flat build b11721, short-chat and the 1K task) re-measured with
# thinking off (budget-mode-rule, 2026-10-19), one job-route sitting of about 50-60 min (the job's anchor phase, then this
# file: the anchor row and three rounds of the two rows). The fix: android/bench/run_cell.py hands a Gemma 4 GGUF row's
# chat template enable_thinking = false (llama-cli ... -st --chat-template-kwargs '{"enable_thinking":false}'); until
# then every Android Gemma 4 reply since 2026-10-05 opened with "[Start thinking]" (docs/dashboard-cells-v1.md "Android
# llama.cpp Gemma 4 thinking (2026-10-19)"). One of four S26 files, run in this order: -s26-e2b, -s26-e4b, -s26-side-e2b,
# -s26-side-e4b (the Pixel 8a runs matrices/dashboard-llama-thinkoff-android.cells).
# The first row is the Android session anchor, byte-identical to matrices/dashboard-llama-b11721-android.cells line 20
# (llama.cpp Qwen3 0.6B short-chat, unchanged by the fix); then the two Gemma 4 E2B rows, each byte-identical to its
# source line: matrices/dashboard-text-v1-android-a.cells lines 28, 31.
# Run after the runner change is on main, the S26 hold taken first by a keeper through the shared queue (the asr lane
# uses the same S26 queue): queue_cli.py enqueue, then queue_cli.py wait <the S26 hold> autopilot_r15_text_e2b <keeper pid>, then
#   BENCH_SITTING=1 python3 scripts/dashboard_job.py s26 --cells matrices/dashboard-llama-thinkoff-s26-e2b.cells --suffix llama-thinkoff-e2b --once --hold-held-by <keeper pid>
# and release the hold when the job ends.

android llama.cpp unsloth/Qwen3-0.6B-GGUF short-chat anchor=1 runs=3 file=Qwen3-0.6B-Q4_K_M.gguf

android llama.cpp unsloth/gemma-4-E2B-it-GGUF short-chat cooldown=300 file=gemma-4-E2B-it-Q4_K_M.gguf
android llama.cpp unsloth/gemma-4-E2B-it-GGUF long-context-1024-gen256 cooldown=300 file=gemma-4-E2B-it-Q4_K_M.gguf context-tokens=2048
